```yaml
rules:
- id: "vuln-dokploy-61cf4266"
  pattern: |>
    if (!memberResult) {
      throw new TRPCError({
        code: "NOT_FOUND",
        message: "User not found in this organization",
      });
    }
    if (memberResult.userId !== ctx.user.id && ctx.user.role !== "owner") {
      throw new TRPCError({
        code: "UNAUTHORIZED",
        message: "You are not authorized to access this user",
      });
    }
  pattern-not: |>
    if (!memberResult) {
      // Fixed version: throw an error if user not found
      throw new Error("User not found in this organization");
    }
    if (memberResult.userId !== ctx.user.id && ctx.user.role !== "owner") {
      // Fixed version: throw an error if user is not authorized
      throw new Error("You are not authorized to access this user");
    }
  languages: ["typescript"]
  message: |>
    **Vulnerability:** Access Control Bypass

    **Description:**
    The code allows unauthorized users to access user information by checking if the user is not found in the organization. This could be exploited by malicious actors to gain unauthorized access to sensitive user data.

    **Solution:**
    Replace the `TRPCError` with a standard `Error` object to throw an error when the user is not found or unauthorized.

    **Severity:** ERROR
```
